# Link patterns lychee must not report.
#
# This file is for a link that is PERMANENTLY UNREACHABLE to a checker while
# still being the right link for a reader -- a host that answers 403 to
# anything without a browser (Confluence does), a page behind a login, a
# template path that resolves only once a file is copied somewhere else. It is
# not a place to silence a link that is simply broken: that one gets fixed.
#
# Every entry states why, on the line above it, and names the run that proved
# it. The nightly `links` job in .github/workflows/ci.yml is what proves it:
# the pull-request lychee run is `--offline` and resolves file-relative links
# only, so it can never be the reason for an entry here. Hostnames that are not
# public at all -- compose service names in example configuration -- are
# `--exclude`d in that job instead, so this file stays a record of what the
# online check found.

# Template links are relative to the future crate README, not this style guide.
/docs/style_guides/docs/(?:design|test_coverage_report)\.md$
